      "writtenOn": "2015-02-24T10:20:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Additionally, keystone IdP identifies a mapping for users coming from a remote IdP. If you associate the same remote IdP with multiple keystone IdP the mapping become ambiguous. The same user could have different policies depending on the log-in link.\n\nThe other way, multiple remote IdPs in a single keystone IdP, makes sense because in this case the mapping is shared and there are not ambiguities.",
      "parentUuid": "ba7be1f8_68560ad4",
      "revId": "da82e15868904d0b11d660c266838ff75f9f2d01",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
