        "id": 8978
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-24T09:15:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you preregister groups like \u0027saml2\u0027, \u0027oidc\u0027 you will also constrain yourself to protocol objects called \u0027saml2\u0027 and \u0027oidc\u0027. As we decided the naming is free we need to keep supporting this freedom. The whole idea behind:\n\n- add a protocol \u0027myawesomeprotocol\u0027\n\nedit keystone.conf and add\n[auth]\nmethods \u003d password,myawesomeprotocol\nmyawesomeprotocol \u003d driver.backend.sql.Protocol\n\nnow, user adds still in the keystone.conf:\n\n[myawesomeprotocol]\nremote_id_attribute \u003d \u0027ParameterNameInClaim\u0027\n\nNow, to be able to to read this value in line 146 we first need to register it.",
      "parentUuid": "ba7be1f8_32b81476",
      "revId": "da82e15868904d0b11d660c266838ff75f9f2d01",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
